# ============================================================================
#  No. 14, the Garnet Arms
# ============================================================================

=== prints
> A press camera in a brown leather case. Tucked inside the lid: a stack of prints, held with a rubber band gone soft.
* [blunt] Look at the prints. -> prints_look
* [warm] Leave them. Augie asked you not to. -> prints_leave

=== prints_look
~ set looked_at_prints
> A bathhouse doorway, shot through rain. A heavy man in a good coat — Alderman Pruitt; his face is on the campaign posters by the El — with his hand on the back of a dockworker's neck. The younger man is laughing. Pruitt is looking at him like he's the only warm thing in the city.
> Neither of them knows the camera is there.
> The next print is the same doorway. Then the same men, closer. Augie wasn't selling this to a jealous wife.
* [cold] Leverage. Somebody would pay a fortune for these. -> prints_cold
* [warm] They look happy. That's the part someone will make them pay for. -> prints_warm
* [wry] Corvane: where the only crime is getting caught. -> prints_wry

=== prints_cold
~ stance cold
> You put them back in order. Mostly.
-> END

=== prints_warm
~ remember ines saw_pruitt_kindly
> You square the edges and slide them back beneath the band, the way they were.
-> END

=== prints_wry
> You put them back. The rubber band snaps on the second try.
-> END

=== prints_leave
> You close the lid without looking. Whatever's in there, it's somebody's life.
~ set respected_prints
-> END

=== ledger
~ set clue.dravo
> A page torn from a collection ledger, in Hobb's square, angry hand. Names, sums, dates. One line is underlined twice:
> "F. DRAVO — cellar under Hu's Laundry, Pell St. — 2 donors Thurs. Paid in full. Do NOT bring them up the front."
? {remnant:silas} -> ledger_silas
-> END

=== ledger_silas
Silas: Donors. Of what? Nobody gives anything in the Sumps, Calder. They get taken.
> [The Sumps and Dravo's cellar are beyond Prototype 1.]
-> END

=== door_2b
? {tenement.cleared} -> door_2b_after
> A radio plays behind the door. The Mercer Quartet, from the Velour, two blocks and a whole world away.
Woman: Whatever he owes, I don't owe it. Go away.
* [warm] I'm not with Hobb. Are you all right in there? -> door_2b_warm
* [cold] Leave it. -> END

=== door_2b_warm
Woman: ...All right? Honey, I'm listening to rich people dance. That's as all right as Number Fourteen gets.
-> END

=== door_2b_after
Woman: It went quiet up there. Did you do that?
* [blunt] Yes. -> door_2b_yes
* [wry] Building's settling. -> door_2b_wry

=== door_2b_yes
~ remember kowal thanked
Woman: Then God keep you, and don't you ever tell anyone I said it.
-> END

=== door_2b_wry
Woman: Settling. Sure. You and me both.
-> END

=== door_1a
> Somebody inside turns the radio louder. That's the whole answer.
-> END
